Chapter: CapGpuFamily
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A denied write returns -1. A granted write returns 0 and the value
 reads back. So "write: 0" and "read: 4242" together mean the family
 grant travelled all the way from the row to the process capability
 word. That is the whole claim.

Section: Body

  gpu-cmd : Integer = #BE000000

  opening : [Gpu, Console] Nothing =
    act
      w <- gpu-mem-write gpu-cmd 0 4242
      print-line-uni ("write: " & show w)
      r <- gpu-mem-read gpu-cmd 0
      print-line-uni ("read: " & show r)
    end

